    "doc": "The 591-byte settings blob a login is answered with (AUTH_SMSG_ACCOUNT_SETTINGS, header 0x0016): the request id, a u16 count, then exactly this many bytes. Copied byte for byte from the reference's own AuthSrv_SendAccountSettings; nothing in this tree knows what most of it means, and it is sent because it is what the reference sends. It is here rather than in code because it is the client's payload: it changes when the reference's blob changes, and a transcribed constant is 591 chances to be silently wrong."
